    <h1>NetAura VPN Account Deletion</h1>
    <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> May 4, 2026</p>

    <p>
        If you use NetAura VPN and want your VPN account and associated backend data deleted,
        you can request deletion by contacting:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> <span class="email">contact.topleveldevelopers@gmail.com</span></li>
        <li><strong>Subject line:</strong> NetAura VPN Account Deletion Request</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Please include enough information for us to identify your account, such as:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>the app name: NetAura VPN</li>
        <li>your VPN account ID, if available</li>
        <li>the email address or contact channel you want us to use to confirm the request</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What happens after a request</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>We will review the request and verify it where needed.</li>
        <li>
            We will delete or anonymize account-related backend data that is no longer required
            for security, fraud prevention, legal compliance, or legitimate operational recordkeeping.
        </li>
        <li>
            Data stored locally on your own device can also be removed by uninstalling the app
            or clearing app storage in Android settings.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Retention exceptions</h2>
    <p>
        We may retain limited information where necessary for legal obligations, abuse prevention,
        fraud prevention, dispute handling, or security investigations.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
        Contact: <span class="email">contact.topleveldevelopers@gmail.com</span>
    </p>

